                "lens": "reliability",
                "location": "engine/review/fsstore/portable.go:24-36",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "On non-linux platforms Lock holds no lock, so the race fixed on linux remains; this is documented in the code, README and CHANGELOG, and the commit scope is explicit. No test covers the portable Lock (not-found and found paths), leaving that branch unproved.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/review/fsstore/portable.go:24-36"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "deterministic",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 10 manifest paths in the candidate patch.",
              "verify.go takes the lock only for blocking verdicts, before spentRound lists stored verdicts, and defers unlock until after the store; the app test asserts the order Lock, Names, Create, Unlock, no lock for non-blocking, and no further store calls when Lock fails.",
              "The linux Lock retries on EINTR, closes the fd on flock failure, and releases by closing; the tests prove mutual exclusion between two Lock calls, not-found without creating directories, symlink refusal, and unsafe feature refusal.",
